<li about="#cite_note-60" id="cite_note-60" data-mw-footnote-number="57"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwBps"><a href="#cite_ref-60" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwBpw"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwBp0">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-60" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt228" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBp4" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"title":{"wt":"Internet Explorer 11 desktop app retirement FAQ"},"url":{"wt":"https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/internet-explorer-11-desktop-app-retirement-faq/ba-p/2366549"},"access-date":{"wt":"13 November 2023"},"language":{"wt":"en"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt228" id="mwBp8"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/internet-explorer-11-desktop-app-retirement-faq/ba-p/2366549" class="external text" id="mwBqA">"Internet Explorer 11 desktop app retirement FAQ"</a><span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwBqE">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwBqI">November 13,</span> 2023</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Internet+Explorer+11+desktop+app+retirement+FAQ&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Ftechcommunity.microsoft.com%2Ft5%2Fwindows-it-pro-blog%2Finternet-explorer-11-desktop-app-retirement-faq%2Fba-p%2F2366549&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AInternet+Explorer" class="Z3988" about="#mwt228" id="mwBqM"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-61" id="cite_note-61" data-mw-footnote-number="58"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwBqQ"><a href="#cite_ref-61" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwBqU"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwBqY">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-61" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt231" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwBqc" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite web ","href":"./Template:Cite_web"},"params":{"url":{"wt":"https://www.theverge.com/tldr/2022/8/3/23290171/how-to-use-internet-explorer-windows-11-why-microsoft-why"},"access-date":{"wt":"22 October 2022"},"last":{"wt":"Warren"},"first":{"wt":"Tom"},"date":{"wt":"3 August 2022"},"title":{"wt":"You can bring Internet Explorer back to life in Windows 11 if you&apos;re a glutton for punishment"},"website":{"wt":"theverge.com"},"publisher":{"wt":"Vox Media, LLC."},"quote":{"wt":"It’s just a matter of searching for Internet Options in the Start menu, launching the control panel applet, selecting the programs tab, hitting “manage add-ons,” and then clicking the “Learn more about toolbars and extensions.” For some reason, this launches Internet Explorer, bypassing the commands that force you into Edge."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFWarren2022" class="citation web cs1" about="#mwt231">Warren, Tom (August 3, 2022). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.theverge.com/tldr/2022/8/3/23290171/how-to-use-internet-explorer-windows-11-why-microsoft-why" class="external text" id="mwBqg">"You can bring Internet Explorer back to life in Windows 11 if you're a glutton for punishment"</a>. <i id="mwBqk">theverge.com</i>. Vox Media, LLC<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwBqo">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwBqs">October 22,</span> 2022</span>. <q id="mwBqw">It's just a matter of searching for Internet Options in the Start menu, launching the control panel applet, selecting the programs tab, hitting "manage add-ons," and then clicking the "Learn more about toolbars and extensions." For some reason, this launches Internet Explorer, bypassing the commands that force you into Edge.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=theverge.com&amp;rft.atitle=You+can+bring+Internet+Explorer+back+to+life+in+Windows+11+if+you%27re+a+glutton+for+punishment&amp;rft.date=2022-08-03&amp;rft.aulast=Warren&amp;rft.aufirst=Tom&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theverge.com%2Ftldr%2F2022%2F8%2F3%2F23290171%2Fhow-to-use-internet-explorer-windows-11-why-microsoft-why&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AInternet+Explorer" class="Z3988" about="#mwt231" id="mwBq0"></span></span></li>
